# References needing a PDF

Every entry in `references.bib` is supposed to end up with a local PDF copy
(`file` field, `docs/references/<bibkey>.pdf`) regardless of whether it also
has a `doi`/`url` — see `harness/roles/researcher.md` "Tooling". This file
is the queue for the ones that don't have one yet: an entry lands here only
after both automated discovery (`harness/tools/find_open_access_pdf.py` —
checks Unpaywall, Semantic Scholar, and arXiv) and a real manual attempt
(publisher page, OA mirror, author site) came up empty.

Work this list when you have time — drop anything you find into
`docs/references/inbox/` as usual and re-run
`harness/tools/intake_references.py`, which resolves the entry and removes
its row here automatically. If you search and come up empty too, say so
(ping the Researcher or note it in `harness/plans/suggestions.md`) so the
entry can move to "Confirmed unavailable" below instead of sitting open
forever.

Each row: bib key — title — doi/url — why the direct attempt failed —
date flagged.

## Open

_(none)_

## Confirmed unavailable (no public copy found — do not cite)

Entries here have no PDF and none is expected to surface. Their content can
never be reverified, so **they must not be cited anywhere**.
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:start -->
That means not in a research memo, not in `docs/theory/`, not in
`docs/report/`.
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:end -->
<!-- SECTION:latex_off:start -->
That means not in a research memo, not in any drafted document.
<!-- SECTION:latex_off:end -->
They stay in `references.bib` as DOI/URL-only entries purely for the record
(existence-checkable), but any draft that leans on one must either find a
verifiable alternate source or drop the claim.
`harness/tools/check_unavailable_sources.py` mechanically enforces this
(run by the Researcher/Author before handoff and by the Reviewer at
verification) — it fails if any tracked key below is cited in
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:start -->
`docs/theory/`, `docs/report/`, or `harness/research/`.
<!-- SECTION:latex_on:end -->
<!-- SECTION:latex_off:start -->
any drafted document or `harness/research/`.
